Give a constant buffer a binding when its block's size is not known until specialization.

The layout of ConstantBuffer<T> and ParameterBlock<T> (source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp) allocates
the buffer's own binding only when the element type "uses ordinary data", which _usesResourceKind
decides as `resInfo->count.compare(0) == std::partial_ordering::greater`. For a block that holds
only an array sized by a specialization constant, the uniform size is LayoutSize::invalid() until
specialization, and an invalid size compares unordered, not greater. The buffer is then treated as
empty: `ConstantBuffer<Block>` with `struct Block { float4 values[kCount]; }` reports no binding of
any kind, the [[vk::push_constant]] form no push-constant range, while the shader reads the buffer.
A block that also has a fixed-size member is bound.

This counts a resource whose size compares unordered as used, so the buffer keeps its binding. A
regression test is added as
tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-specialization-sized-constant-buffer-binding.cpp.

Measured on v2026.21, all four platforms: no parameter category reported for the buffer.
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp b/source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp
index 1af403475..455a80267 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-type-layout.cpp
@@ -3890,7 +3890,15 @@ IRVarLayout* applyOffsetToVarLayout(
 static bool _usesResourceKind(RefPtr<TypeLayout> typeLayout, LayoutResourceKind kind)
 {
     auto resInfo = typeLayout->FindResourceInfo(kind);
-    return resInfo && resInfo->count.compare(0) == std::partial_ordering::greater;
+    if (!resInfo)
+        return false;
+
+    // A count that does not compare with 0 is one not known until specialization (an array sized
+    // by a specialization constant): the type still uses the resource. Treating it as unused
+    // dropped the constant buffer of a block holding only such arrays, binding and all.
+    //
+    auto order = resInfo->count.compare(0);
+    return order == std::partial_ordering::greater || order == std::partial_ordering::unordered;
 }
 
 static bool _usesOrdinaryData(RefPtr<TypeLayout> typeLayout)
